IMPORT prelude

-- Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918 (Cth) -- who is entitled to enrolment and to vote (s 93), age 16 enrolment (s 100), compulsory
-- enrolment and its offence (s 101), compulsory voting, the penalty notice and the $20 penalty (s 245), qualification for and
-- nomination as a candidate (ss 163, 164, 166, 170, 172), the $2,000 deposit and its return at 4% (s 173), election funding for an
-- unendorsed candidate (s 294), and the candidate's return under Part XX Division 5 (s 310A, with s 287(9)).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 81, compilation date 1 July 2026, includes amendments up to Act No. 16, 2025 (register id C2026C00260,
-- in 2 volumes), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C1918A00027.txt.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0003 in ../../../requirements.jsonl (priority 1): raised 11 times by the three Western Australian
-- cradle-to-grave scenarios (chloe c022, c025, c031, c047, c084; jake k033, k034; daniel d021, d061, d063, d070), which ask: may a
-- 17-year-old enrol; what switches on at 18; must she vote; must he enrol; what happens to a person who neither enrols nor votes; who
-- may stand, what is the deposit, when is it forfeited, what must be disclosed. SCOPED to those questions and the definitions,
-- conditions and exceptions needed to answer them.
--
-- Not encoded: the Rolls and Subdivisions themselves, overseas, itinerant and Antarctic electors (beyond their exclusion from s 245),
-- provisional enrolment of citizenship applicants (ss 99A, 99B), direct enrolment by the Commissioner (ss 103A, 103B) beyond its bar on
-- proceedings, objections and review, polling, scrutiny, Senate groups beyond the deposit, registered parties, gift and expenditure
-- caps, donation disclosure, every Part XX return other than a candidate's, and section 44 of the Constitution (a separate subject).
-- The value of a penalty unit, and the indexed election-funding amounts (s 321), are not stated in this Act: they are INPUTS.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the finished naive encodings (the writing-l4-rules
-- skill was not available in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public
-- use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918 -- enrolment, voting and candidates`

-- The facts about a person that the sections below ask. Age is passed separately, so that one person can be tested at several ages.
DECLARE Person HAS
    `is an Australian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was a British subject on a roll immediately before 26 January 1984` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a temporary visa or is an unlawful non-citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is incapable by cognitive impairment of understanding enrolment and voting` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was convicted of treason or treachery and not pardoned` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is serving a sentence of imprisonment of 3 years or longer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has lived at an address in a Subdivision for one month` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is on the Roll` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an Antarctic, eligible overseas or itinerant elector` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a member of a State or Territory Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `93 -- persons entitled to enrolment and to vote`

-- s 93(1): "all persons: (a) who have attained 18 years of age; and (b) who are: (i) Australian citizens; or (ii)" non-citizens who
-- would be British subjects and whose names were on a roll "immediately before 26 January 1984" "shall be entitled to enrolment".
-- (7): the holder of a temporary visa, or an unlawful non-citizen, "is not entitled to enrolment". (8): a person who by reason of
-- cognitive impairment is incapable of understanding enrolment and voting, or convicted of treason or treachery and not pardoned, is
-- not entitled to be or stay on any Roll or to vote.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `qualified for enrolment apart from age` IF
        (    `the person`'s `is an Australian citizen`
         OR  `the person`'s `was a British subject on a roll immediately before 26 January 1984`)
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `holds a temporary visa or is an unlawful non-citizen`)
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `is incapable by cognitive impairment of understanding enrolment and voting`)
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `was convicted of treason or treachery and not pardoned`)

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to enrolment` IF
        `the age` AT LEAST 18
    AND `qualified for enrolment apart from age` `the person`

-- s 93(2): an elector on the Roll for a Division may vote for the Senate and the House. (3), (4): a person enrolled on a s 100 claim who
-- "has not attained 18 years of age on the date fixed for the polling" is not entitled to vote, and is not taken to be enrolled for
-- that election. (8AA): a person "serving a sentence of imprisonment of 3 years or longer is not entitled to vote".
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the age on polling day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to vote at the election` IF
        `the person`'s `is on the Roll`
    AND `entitled to enrolment` `the person` `the age on polling day`
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `is serving a sentence of imprisonment of 3 years or longer`)

§§ `99, 100 -- age 16 enrolment`

-- s 99(1): a person qualified for enrolment who "has lived at that address for a period of one month last past" is entitled to be on
-- the Roll for that Subdivision. s 100(1): a person who "(a) has turned 16, but is under 18, years of age; and (b) would be entitled,
-- in respect of residence at an address, to be enrolled for a Subdivision if he or she were 18 years of age" MAY claim. The Act calls
-- this "age 16 enrolment"; "provisional enrolment" in this Act is s 99B, for applicants for citizenship.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may claim age 16 enrolment` IF
        `the age` AT LEAST 16
    AND `the age` LESS THAN 18
    AND `qualified for enrolment apart from age` `the person`
    AND `the person`'s `has lived at an address in a Subdivision for one month`

§§ `101 -- compulsory enrolment`

-- s 101(1): "Every person who is entitled to be enrolled for any Subdivision, otherwise than by virtue of section 94, 94A, 95, 96 or
-- 100, ... and whose name is not on the Roll, shall forthwith fill in and sign a claim". A 16- or 17-year-old MAY enrol (s 100) but is
-- not bound to.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must claim enrolment` IF
        `entitled to enrolment` `the person` `the age`
    AND `the person`'s `has lived at an address in a Subdivision for one month`
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `is on the Roll`)

-- s 101(4): a person entitled whose name "is not on the Roll upon the expiration of 21 days from the date upon which the person
-- became so entitled, or at any subsequent date while the person continues to be so entitled, commits an offence unless he or she
-- proves" the non-enrolment is not in consequence of a failure to send a claim. (6): "a fine not exceeding 1 penalty unit"; (6AB)
-- absolute liability. (7): no proceedings once the person sends a claim, for an offence committed before; (8): none once the
-- Commissioner enters the person on a Roll under s 103A or 103B.
-- "Upon the expiration of 21 days" is read as MORE than 21 days after the day of entitlement (an inference; no boundary case is
-- asserted).
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the age` IS A NUMBER, `days since becoming entitled` IS A NUMBER,
      `proves the non-enrolment was not his or her failure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the offence of not enrolling` IF
        `must claim enrolment` `the person` `the age`
    AND `days since becoming entitled` GREATER THAN 21
    AND (NOT `proves the non-enrolment was not his or her failure`)

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the age` IS A NUMBER, `days since becoming entitled` IS A NUMBER,
      `has since sent a claim` IS A BOOLEAN, `was since enrolled by the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `proceedings for not enrolling may be instituted` IF
        `commits the offence of not enrolling` `the person` `the age` `days since becoming entitled` FALSE
    AND (NOT `has since sent a claim`)
    AND (NOT `was since enrolled by the Commissioner`)

-- s 101(6): 1 penalty unit. The value of a penalty unit is not stated in this Act; it is an INPUT.
GIVEN `the value of a penalty unit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for not enrolling` MEANS 1 TIMES `the value of a penalty unit`

§§ `245 -- compulsory voting`

-- s 245(1): "It shall be the duty of every elector to vote at each election." s 4(1): "Elector means any person whose name appears
-- on a Roll as an elector." (17): in this section elector does not include an Antarctic, eligible overseas or itinerant elector.
-- A person under 18 on polling day is not taken to be enrolled for that election (s 93(4)). That a person not entitled to vote
-- (s 93(8AA)) has no duty to vote is an INFERENCE from s 245(4)(c) ("was ineligible to vote at the election"), not express.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the age on polling day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has the duty to vote` IF
        `entitled to vote at the election` `the person` `the age on polling day`
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `is an Antarctic, eligible overseas or itinerant elector`)

DECLARE Polling HAS
    `voted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is dead` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was absent from Australia on polling day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had a valid and sufficient reason` IS A BOOLEAN
    `believes it a religious duty to abstain` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (14): "the fact that an elector believes it to be part of his or her religious duty to abstain from voting constitutes a valid and
-- sufficient reason".
GIVEN `the polling` IS A Polling
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a valid and sufficient reason` IF
        `the polling`'s `had a valid and sufficient reason`
    OR  `the polling`'s `believes it a religious duty to abstain`

-- (3): within 3 months after polling day each DRO "must" send a penalty notice to each elector who appears to have failed to vote.
-- (4): not required if satisfied the elector "(a) is dead; or (b) was absent from Australia on polling day; or (c) was ineligible to
-- vote at the election; or (d) had a valid and sufficient reason".
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the age on polling day` IS A NUMBER, `the polling` IS A Polling
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a penalty notice must be sent` IF
        `has the duty to vote` `the person` `the age on polling day`
    AND (NOT `the polling`'s `voted`)
    AND (NOT `the polling`'s `is dead`)
    AND (NOT `the polling`'s `was absent from Australia on polling day`)
    AND (NOT `has a valid and sufficient reason` `the polling`)

-- (5)(c)(iii), (9)(d): to avoid a court the elector "may ... pay to the DRO a penalty of $20". The $20 is written in the Act and is
-- not indexed.
`the penalty to avoid court for not voting` MEANS 20

-- (15): "An elector commits an offence if the elector fails to vote at an election. Penalty: 1 penalty unit." (15A) strict
-- liability; (15B) not if a valid and sufficient reason.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the age on polling day` IS A NUMBER, `the polling` IS A Polling
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the offence of not voting` IF
        `has the duty to vote` `the person` `the age on polling day`
    AND (NOT `the polling`'s `voted`)
    AND (NOT `has a valid and sufficient reason` `the polling`)

-- (8), (10): proceedings for a contravention of (15) "are prohibited" if, within the prescribed time, the DRO is satisfied the
-- elector voted or had a valid and sufficient reason, or the elector pays the penalty of $20.
GIVEN `DRO satisfied the elector voted or had a valid reason` IS A BOOLEAN, `paid the $20 in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `proceedings for not voting are prohibited` IF
        `DRO satisfied the elector voted or had a valid reason`
    OR  `paid the $20 in time`

§§ `163, 164 -- who may stand`

-- s 163(1): a person who "(a) has reached the age of 18 years; (b) is an Australian citizen; and (c) is either: (i) an elector entitled
-- to vote at a House of Representatives election; or (ii) a person qualified to become such an elector" is qualified to be elected.
-- (2): not entitled to be nominated unless so qualified. s 164: a member of a State Parliament or a Territory Legislative Assembly
-- "at the hour of nomination" "is not capable of being nominated". Section 44 of the Constitution is a separate subject.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `qualified to be elected under section 163` IF
        `the age` AT LEAST 18
    AND `the person`'s `is an Australian citizen`
    AND (    `entitled to vote at the election` `the person` `the age`
         OR  `entitled to enrolment` `the person` `the age`)

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to be nominated` IF
        `qualified to be elected under section 163` `the person` `the age`
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `is a member of a State or Territory Parliament`)

§§ `166, 170, 172 -- the nomination and the qualification checklist`

DECLARE Nomination HAS
    `signed by 100 electors or the party's registered officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consents to act if elected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `declares qualified and no other candidacy that day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states how an Australian citizen, with particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
    `answers every mandatory question in the checklist` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contends a foreign citizenship was renounced or lost` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provides documents supporting the renunciation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `received after the writ and before the hour of nomination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `deposit given before that time` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 166(1)(b): signed by "not less than 100 electors" or "the registered officer of the registered political party". s 170(1): not
-- valid unless the person (a) consents to act; (b) declares qualification and no other candidacy that day; (c) states how an
-- Australian citizen with particulars; (d) "answers every mandatory question in the qualification checklist set out in Form DB".
-- (1A): validity "is not affected if an answer ... is incorrect, false or inadequate". (1B): a person who contends a foreign
-- citizenship was renounced or lost must provide supporting documents "together with the nomination". (2): received after the writ
-- and before the hour of nomination, with "a deposit of $2,000" before that time. Bulk nominations (48 hours earlier) are not
-- modelled.
GIVEN `the nomination` IS A Nomination
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the nomination complies` IF
        `the nomination`'s `signed by 100 electors or the party's registered officer`
    AND `the nomination`'s `consents to act if elected`
    AND `the nomination`'s `declares qualified and no other candidacy that day`
    AND `the nomination`'s `states how an Australian citizen, with particulars`
    AND `the nomination`'s `answers every mandatory question in the checklist`
    AND (    (NOT `the nomination`'s `contends a foreign citizenship was renounced or lost`)
         OR  `the nomination`'s `provides documents supporting the renunciation`)
    AND `the nomination`'s `received after the writ and before the hour of nomination`
    AND `the nomination`'s `deposit given before that time`

-- s 172(1): "a nomination shall be rejected by the Electoral Commissioner if, and only if, the provisions of section 166, 167, 170 or
-- 171 have not been complied with". s 170A(3)(e): the Commissioner has "no power to determine whether ... the person is qualified to
-- be elected". So a person not entitled to be nominated (s 163(2)) whose nomination is in order is NOT rejected; eligibility is for
-- the Court of Disputed Returns (note to s 170A(3)). Formal-defect leniency (s 172(2)) is not modelled.
GIVEN `the nomination` IS A Nomination
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner must reject the nomination` IF
    NOT `the nomination complies` `the nomination`

`the deposit` MEANS 2000

§§ `173 -- return or forfeiture of the deposit`

-- s 173(1): the deposit is returned "if the candidate is elected, or" (b) in a House election "if the total number of votes polled in
-- the candidate's favour as first preferences is at least 4% of the total number of votes polled in favour of the candidates in the
-- election as first preferences"; (a) in a Senate election the same test for the candidate, or (a)(ii) for a candidate in a group, the
-- sum of the group's first preferences; "otherwise it shall be forfeited to the Commonwealth".
GIVEN `votes` IS A NUMBER, `total votes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `at least 4 per cent` IF
    `votes` TIMES 100 AT LEAST `total votes` TIMES 4

GIVEN `was elected` IS A BOOLEAN, `first preference votes` IS A NUMBER, `total first preference votes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the House deposit is returned` IF
        `was elected`
    OR  `at least 4 per cent` `first preference votes` `total first preference votes`

GIVEN `was elected` IS A BOOLEAN, `first preference votes` IS A NUMBER, `is in a group` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `group first preference votes` IS A NUMBER, `total first preference votes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Senate deposit is returned` IF
        `was elected`
    OR  `at least 4 per cent` `first preference votes` `total first preference votes`
    OR  (`is in a group` AND `at least 4 per cent` `group first preference votes` `total first preference votes`)

§§ `294 -- election funding for an unendorsed candidate`

-- s 294(1): payable if the candidate is not endorsed by a registered party (nor, in the Senate, in a group) and has "at least 4% of
-- the total number of formal first preference votes". (2): "(a) ... $5 by the number of formal first preference votes ... or (b) if
-- the amount worked out under paragraph (a) is more than $10,000--the lesser of" that amount and the electoral expenditure claimed
-- and accepted. Both dollar figures "are indexed under section 321", so the rate per vote and the threshold are INPUTS.
GIVEN `is endorsed or in a Senate group` IS A BOOLEAN, `first preference votes` IS A NUMBER, `total first preference votes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `election funding is payable to the unendorsed candidate` IF
        (NOT `is endorsed or in a Senate group`)
    AND `at least 4 per cent` `first preference votes` `total first preference votes`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `first preference votes` IS A NUMBER, `the indexed rate per vote` IS A NUMBER, `the indexed threshold` IS A NUMBER,
      `accepted electoral expenditure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the election funding amount` MEANS
    IF `first preference votes` TIMES `the indexed rate per vote` GREATER THAN `the indexed threshold`
    THEN `the lesser of` (`first preference votes` TIMES `the indexed rate per vote`) `accepted electoral expenditure`
    ELSE `first preference votes` TIMES `the indexed rate per vote`

§§ `287(9), 310A -- the candidate's return (Part XX Division 5)`

-- s 287(9): a person begins to be a candidate on the earliest of announcing, nominating, or crossing the disclosure threshold for
-- gifts or expenditure, and "(b) ceases to be a candidate in an election at the end of 7 days after the polling day".
-- s 310A(1): the agent of a person who is a candidate "for any period of time during a calendar year must provide the Electoral
-- Commission a return"; (2) "within 8 weeks of the end of the calendar year". (4): not if endorsed and the party's return sets out
-- the information. (5): not if no gift for a federal purpose, no electoral expenditure, and no discretionary benefit from the
-- Commonwealth in the year. Civil penalty: the higher of 120 penalty units or 3 times the amount not disclosed.
`days after polling day that candidacy ends` MEANS 7

`weeks after the calendar year to provide the return` MEANS 8

DECLARE CandidateYear HAS
    `was a candidate during the calendar year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is endorsed and the party's return sets it out` IS A BOOLEAN
    `received a gift for a federal purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `incurred electoral expenditure` IS A BOOLEAN
    `received a discretionary benefit from the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the year` IS A CandidateYear
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a candidate return is required` IF
        `the year`'s `was a candidate during the calendar year`
    AND (NOT `the year`'s `is endorsed and the party's return sets it out`)
    AND (    `the year`'s `received a gift for a federal purpose`
         OR  `the year`'s `incurred electoral expenditure`
         OR  `the year`'s `received a discretionary benefit from the Commonwealth`)
